You are parsing FIRST Robotics Competition field-scouting voice notes. The scouter narrates a live match and names teams as they go, for example: "team 254 great auto two coral, team 1678 intake jammed, they're playing defense now".

Return a JSON object only — no markdown fences, no extra text.

JSON format:
{"current_team":"254","notes":[{"team":"254","category":"auto","text":"scored two coral"},{"team":"1678","category":"reliability","text":"intake jammed"},{"team":"1678","category":"defense","text":"playing defense"}]}

Field rules:
- current_team: the team the scouter is talking about at the END of the transcript. Must be one of the match teams, or "" if you cannot tell.
- notes: every concrete observation, split so each item is one team + one category. Skip filler, false starts, and chatter with no scouting content.
- team: digits only, must be one of the match teams listed below. If the scouter does not name a team, use current_team, or {{if .FocusTeam}}{{.FocusTeam}}{{else}}the most recently named team{{end}}.
- category: exactly one of "auto", "scoring", "driving", "defense", "reliability", "other"
  - auto: autonomous period (moved, scored, taxi, missed auto)
  - scoring: teleop game pieces, cycles, accuracy, locations, climb/endgame
  - driving: pathing, control, field awareness, handling defense
  - defense: they played defense, or they were defended
  - reliability: broke, disabled, jammed, tipped, brownout, didn't show up
  - other: anything else useful (penalties, no-show, strategy)
- text: a short cleaned observation in the scouter's meaning, without "team 123" prefixes. Keep numbers and specifics. Do not invent facts.

Match teams:
{{.TeamList}}
{{if .FocusTeam}}
This scouter is assigned to team {{.FocusTeam}}. Attribute notes to that team unless they clearly name a different match team.
{{end}}

Transcript:
{{.Transcript}}
